.nh
.TH "SYMVAULT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Symaira Vault" "Symaira Vault Manual"

.SH NAME
symvault-migrate-session - Upgrade a cached session from the legacy plaintext format to encrypted


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsymvault migrate session [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Upgrade a cached session from the legacy plaintext format to the
encrypted form that uses a randomly generated wrap key.

.PP
Earlier versions of Symaira Vault stored cached passphrases in plaintext
inside the OS keyring. The current implementation refuses to transparently
load a legacy plaintext session; run this command once per vault to
upgrade the cached entry.

.PP
The migration is a no-op when the session is already in the encrypted
format. The vault directory defaults to the value of --vault (or the
$SYMVAULT_VAULT environment variable).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview the migration without writing

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for session


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	When to emit ANSI color: auto, always, never

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output format shorthand for --output json; overrides --output when both are specified

.PP
\fB--no-pipe-warning\fP[=false]
	suppress 'reading from non-TTY' warning when piping secrets

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format (text, json, yaml)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	use a named vault profile

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB--theme\fP=""
	Color preset: default, highcontrast, colorblind (or SYMVAULT_THEME)

.PP
\fB--vault\fP="~/.symvault"
	path to the password vault


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  symvault migrate session
  symvault migrate session --vault ~/.symvault
  symvault migrate session --dry-run
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsymvault-migrate(1)\fP
